  "body": "<<HEAD dateModified=\"2026-07-03T11:40:00+00:00\">>\n        <p class=\"ssr-meta\">Area Forecast Discussion · National Weather Service Los Angeles (LOX) · issued <time datetime=\"2026-07-03T11:40:00+00:00\">Friday, July 3 at 4:40 AM PDT</time>.</p>\n        <p class=\"ssr-changelog\">Revised in 1 passage since the 10:38 PM discussion. <a href=\"/o/LOX/?view=changelog\">See every revision</a>.</p>\n        <article class=\"forecast-section ssr\">\n            <h2 class=\"section-title\">Synopsis</h2>\n            <p>Low clouds and fog will continue each night and morning with a chance of drizzle near the coasts through the weekend across the region.</p>\n        </article>\n        <article class=\"forecast-section ssr\">\n            <h2 class=\"section-title\">Short Term</h2>\n            <p>Marine layer around 1500 feet deep this morning. A wknd warming trend is expected as high pressure builds over the region with temperatures above normal in the valleys by Saturday afternoon and evening.</p>\n        </article>\n        <article class=\"forecast-section ssr\">\n            <h2 class=\"section-title\">Long Term</h2>\n            <p>Models are in good agreement that troughing returns early next week bringing a cooling trend and increasing onshore flow across the area.</p>\n        </article>\n        <p class=\"ssr-note\">This is the plain-text edition, decoded without AI so it loads anywhere. The full Plaincast experience — plain-English summaries beside the annotated original, with the <a href=\"/o/LOX/?view=changelog\">forecast changelog</a> — loads automatically with JavaScript.</p>\n    <<MID>><script type=\"application/json\" id=\"plaincast-boot\">{\"v\":1,\"office\":\"LOX\",\"product\":{\"id\":\"golden-curr-0001\",\"issuanceTime\":\"2026-07-03T11:40:00+00:00\",\"productText\":\"000\\nFXUS66 KLOX 031140\\nAFDLOX\\n\\nArea Forecast Discussion\\nNational Weather Service Los Angeles/Oxnard CA\\n440 AM PDT Thu Jul 3 2026\\n\\n.SYNOPSIS...03/440 AM.\\nLow clouds and fog will continue each night and morning with a chc of\\ndrizzle near the csts through the weekend across the region.\\n\\n\\u0026\\u0026\\n\\n.SHORT TERM (Today through Saturday)...\\nMarine layer around 1500 feet deep this morning. A wknd warming trend\\nis expected as high pressure builds over the region with temps abv\\nnormal in the vlys by Saturday afternoon and evening.\\n\\n\\u0026\\u0026\\n\\n.LONG TERM (Sunday through Wednesday)...\\nModels are in good agreement that troughing returns early next week\\nbringing a cooling trend and increasing onshore flow across the area.\\n\\n\\u0026\\u0026\\n\\n.AVIATION...03/1140Z. VFR.\\n\\n$$\\n\"},\"translations\":{\"Short Term\":\"A **warming trend** this weekend, with valley highs above normal by **Saturday**.\"},\"translationsComplete\":true,\"changelog\":{\"changelog\":\"Warmer this weekend.\",\"since\":\"2026-07-03T05:38:00+00:00\",\"updated\":\"2026-07-03T11:40:00+00:00\"}}</script>\n    <<SCRIPT>><<TAIL>>"
